1
00:00:01,196 --> 00:00:02,731
Welcome to the Shark Cage!

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:04,810
A million dollars on the line...

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,210
and across the table sits the most feared

4
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,250
man in poker.

5
00:00:09,123 --> 00:00:10,650
Phil. Ivey.

6
00:00:11,854 --> 00:00:15,124
Ace-queen. Suited. Ooh, that's pretty.

7
00:00:15,385 --> 00:00:17,315
Ivey raises from under the gun.

8
00:00:17,168 --> 00:00:18,915
Thirty-eight thousand.

9
00:00:19,131 --> 00:00:21,017
Ace-queen suited, on the button?

10
00:00:21,007 --> 00:00:22,857
I'm not folding this.

11
00:00:22,687 --> 00:00:23,337
Call.

12
00:00:23,735 --> 00:00:26,818
Quick lesson. Ace-queen suited is one of the

13
00:00:26,648 --> 00:00:28,938
ten best starting hands.

14
00:00:28,753 --> 00:00:31,458
Against an early raise, calling on the button

15
00:00:31,235 --> 00:00:34,738
is great. A three-bet is fine too.

16
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:38,222
The flop! Eight...

17
00:00:38,012 --> 00:00:39,822
eight... ACE!

18
00:00:39,969 --> 00:00:42,555
Aces up! Two pair, queen kicker.

19
00:00:42,625 --> 00:00:45,435
I'm basically a genius.

20
00:00:45,858 --> 00:00:48,197
On an eight, eight, ace flop, you have

21
00:00:47,987 --> 00:00:51,077
aces up. That's a strong hand, so betting

22
00:00:50,867 --> 00:00:52,437
for value is right.

23
00:00:52,663 --> 00:00:55,633
He checks. Let's bet fifty thousand.

24
00:00:55,657 --> 00:00:57,987
And Ivey... calls.

25
00:00:57,977 --> 00:01:00,227
No emotion. None.

26
00:01:01,164 --> 00:01:02,787
Is he even breathing?

27
00:01:03,424 --> 00:01:05,994
The turn. A seven.

28
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,130
He checks again.

29
00:01:07,160 --> 00:01:08,650
I'll check too.

30
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:12,170
Pot control. Very professional.

31
00:01:12,689 --> 00:01:15,081
Checking the turn keeps the pot small, and

32
00:01:14,871 --> 00:01:16,761
gives Ivey a chance to bluff.

33
00:01:17,603 --> 00:01:19,773
The river... a nine.

34
00:01:19,663 --> 00:01:21,373
And Ivey checks.

35
00:01:21,263 --> 00:01:23,693
For the third time.

36
00:01:24,027 --> 00:01:25,005
Be careful though.

37
00:01:24,888 --> 00:01:27,645
Three checks don't always mean weak.

38
00:01:27,542 --> 00:01:30,765
Great players check their monsters to set a

39
00:01:30,611 --> 00:01:31,405
trap.

40
00:01:31,749 --> 00:01:33,706
Three checks. He's weak.

41
00:01:33,536 --> 00:01:35,386
He HAS to be weak.

42
00:01:35,296 --> 00:01:38,106
A hundred and twenty-five thousand.

43
00:01:38,653 --> 00:01:41,080
And Phil Ivey...

44
00:01:40,897 --> 00:01:47,480
check-raises... to FOUR HUNDRED AND FIFTY THOUSAND!

45
00:01:48,108 --> 00:01:50,246
Wait. What. WHY.

46
00:01:50,103 --> 00:01:51,926
He checked three times!

47
00:01:51,852 --> 00:01:54,406
Okay, think. What beats me?

48
00:01:54,556 --> 00:01:59,286
Aces... ace-eight... any eight...

49
00:01:59,084 --> 00:02:00,406
jack-ten...

50
00:02:00,818 --> 00:02:01,957
So what beats you here?

51
00:02:02,067 --> 00:02:05,717
Aces. Ace-eight. Any eight.

52
00:02:05,627 --> 00:02:07,557
Nines or sevens full.

53
00:02:07,507 --> 00:02:11,557
Ace-king. Jack-ten. Ten-six.

54
00:02:11,487 --> 00:02:14,757
And a river check-raise from Ivey is usually

55
00:02:14,547 --> 00:02:15,717
one of those.

56
00:02:16,469 --> 00:02:17,789
Now the math.

57
00:02:17,639 --> 00:02:20,429
You have to call three hundred twenty-five thousand

58
00:02:20,312 --> 00:02:23,149
to win one point one million.

59
00:02:23,059 --> 00:02:25,389
So you need to be right about thirty

60
00:02:25,189 --> 00:02:26,669
percent of the time.

61
00:02:27,223 --> 00:02:28,500
Would YOU call?

62
00:02:31,490 --> 00:02:32,820
I've come this far.

63
00:02:33,010 --> 00:02:35,140
I... call.

64
00:02:36,656 --> 00:02:39,898
ACES! Phil Ivey has ACES FULL!

65
00:02:39,755 --> 00:02:42,378
He trapped her the ENTIRE hand!

66
00:02:42,847 --> 00:02:44,374
Cool. Cool cool cool.

67
00:02:46,643 --> 00:02:50,013
The lesson? Ace-queen is a great hand.

68
00:02:49,863 --> 00:02:52,333
But against a player like Ivey, you're not

69
00:02:52,123 --> 00:02:54,013
getting three streets of value.

70
00:02:53,863 --> 00:02:56,812
And when he check-raises the river...

71
00:02:56,624 --> 00:02:58,501
he usually has it.

72
00:02:59,469 --> 00:03:00,879
Would YOU have called?

73
00:03:00,805 --> 00:03:02,799
Tell me in the comments.

74
00:03:02,609 --> 00:03:06,719
And subscribe... or Ivey will check-raise you too.
